# 2. PRODUCT VISION

The platform should allow an administrator to create AI agents that can behave like natural human telephone assistants.

Examples of intended applications:

- AI receptionist.
- Customer support representative.
- Appointment booking assistant.
- Sales assistant.
- Lead qualification agent.
- Business information assistant.
- Customer follow-up agent.
- Order status assistant.
- General-purpose AI telephone assistant.

The AI must be capable of:

- Receiving incoming calls.
- Making outgoing calls.
- Listening to natural speech.
- Understanding conversational context.
- Responding naturally through generated speech.
- Handling interruptions.
- Recognizing when someone has finished speaking.
- Asking relevant follow-up questions.
- Remembering information within the active conversation.
- Accessing configured business knowledge.
- Transferring calls to human representatives.
- Ending conversations appropriately.

The system must not force conversations into rigid question-and-answer sequences unless the administrator specifically configures such a workflow.

