# 12. INCOMING TELEPHONE CALLS

Build a complete inbound calling module.

## Required functionality

- Connect a supported telephony provider.
- Register or configure phone numbers.
- Receive incoming call webhooks.
- Verify webhook signatures.
- Identify the destination number.
- Identify the associated organization.
- Identify the assigned AI agent.
- Initialize a real-time voice session.
- Connect caller audio to the voice engine.
- Stream generated AI audio back to the caller.
- Handle call disconnection.
- Save call records.
- Save transcripts.
- Generate summaries.

## Incoming call flow

1. A caller dials the configured number.
2. Telephony provider receives the call.
3. Laravel verifies the incoming webhook.
4. The platform identifies the destination and assigned agent.
5. The voice engine creates a session.
6. The AI begins the configured greeting.
7. The conversation continues naturally.
8. The AI completes the task or transfers the call.
9. The call ends.
10. The platform saves the final call information.

Support multiple concurrent incoming calls within configured capacity.

Do not assume every telephony provider has identical audio streaming functionality.

