# 28. FINAL DEFINITION OF DONE

The project is considered successfully delivered when it is a genuinely usable AI Calling Agent platform, not merely a prototype.

The administrator must be able to:

1. Log in.
2. Configure AI provider credentials.
3. Test provider connectivity.
4. Configure a telephony provider.
5. Create an AI agent.
6. Select its voice, language and personality.
7. Add custom instructions.
8. Add business knowledge.
9. Open the browser voice playground.
10. Speak directly to the agent.
11. Hear natural AI responses.
12. Interrupt the AI naturally.
13. Review conversation transcripts.
14. Assign the agent to a phone number.
15. Receive real telephone calls.
16. Make real telephone calls.
17. Manage calling campaigns.
18. Review call recordings where enabled and consented to.
19. Review call costs and usage.
20. Manage users and permissions.
21. Monitor system health.
22. Configure and switch compatible AI providers.

The application must support both low-cost/self-hosted and paid configurations, with clear instructions and honest limitations.

The most important quality objective is natural, fast and reliable voice interaction.

Do not sacrifice conversational quality for a large collection of unfinished features.

**Priority order:**

1. Reliable real-time voice engine.
2. Natural conversational experience.
3. Working browser voice playground.
4. Working incoming and outgoing telephone calls.
5. Easy provider and agent configuration.
6. Knowledge base and human handoff.
7. Usage management and analytics.
8. Advanced features and integrations.

Build a solid foundation first, then expand it.

**Start by inspecting the existing repository and presenting the implementation plan. Do not generate the entire application in one uncontrolled batch.**
